Let $\frac{S}{n}$ represent the sum of each row in the $\frac{1}{p}$-array, where $S$ is the sum of the first terms of each row, and $n$ is an integer to be determined. Considering a row with first term $\frac{a}{p}$, where $a \in \mathbb{Z}^+$, then the $n$ th row will have first term
\begin{align*} \frac{a}{p}\cdot(\frac{1}{p})^{n-1}=\frac{a}{p+n-1}
\end{align*}

